---
import TrainingLayout from "../../layouts/TrainingLayout.astro";
import Snippet from "../../components/training/Snippet.astro";
import LiveDemo from "../../components/training/LiveDemo.astro";
import ApiLink from "../../components/training/ApiLink.astro";
import ChapterLink from "../../components/training/ChapterLink.astro";
import Callout from "../../components/training/Callout.astro";
import { Code } from "astro-expressive-code/components";
---
<TrainingLayout slug="selection-and-copy">

  <h2 id="model">A selection model per table</h2>
  <p>
    What can be selected is decided by a <ApiLink name="SelectionModel" />. It takes a type
    (<ApiLink name="ExtendedSelectionType" />) and a mode (<ApiLink name="SelectionMode" />):
  </p>
  <Snippet file="demos/selection-and-copy.ts" region="options" />
  <table>
    <thead><tr><th>Type</th><th>A click selects …</th></tr></thead>
    <tbody>
      <tr><td><code>"cell"</code></td><td>one cell</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>"row"</code> / <code>"column"</code></td><td>the whole row / column</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>"range"</code></td><td>one cell – or a rectangle: drag with the mouse or Shift+click</td></tr>
      <tr><td><code>"none"</code></td><td>nothing</td></tr>
    </tbody>
  </table>
  <p>Mode <code>"multi"</code> adds more selections with ⌘/Ctrl+click; <code>"single"</code> replaces the selection.
    ⌘/Ctrl+click on a selected cell deselects it, ⌘/Ctrl+Alt+click removes a cell from the selection.</p>

  <h2 id="keyboard">Mouse and keyboard</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>Drag = range (since 1.1.88), <kbd>⌘/Ctrl</kbd>+drag = another range, <kbd>Shift</kbd>+click = range from the last
      click up to here (click again with <kbd>Shift</kbd> to change it), <kbd>⌘/Ctrl</kbd>+click = another cell.</li>
    <li><kbd>⌘/Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd> copies, <kbd>⌘/Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>A</kbd> selects all (<kbd>⌘/Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>A</kbd>,
      <kbd>⌘/Ctrl</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd> copies the whole displayed body, up to <code>CopyService.maxCopyCells</code> cells), arrow keys move the focus.</li>
    <li>Shortcuts can be remapped or switched off (<code>shortcutActionIdMapping</code>, <code>shortcutActionsDisabled</code> in
      <ApiLink name="TableOptionsIf" />).</li>
  </ul>

  <h2 id="events">React to the selection</h2>
  <Snippet file="demos/selection-and-copy.ts" region="events" />
  <p>
    <ApiLink name="EventListenerIf.onSelectionChanged" /> gets the model (once per click); <ApiLink name="SelectionModelIf.getRanges" />
    returns the selected rectangles (<code>r1, c1, r2, c2</code> – for rows and columns unbounded, so count rows with
    <ApiLink name="SelectionModelIf.getMergedRowIndices" />). Event listeners in general: <ChapterLink slug="events-and-context-menu" />.
  </p>

  <h2 id="copy">Copy</h2>
  <Snippet file="demos/selection-and-copy.ts" region="copy" />
  <p>
    <ApiLink name="TableApi.copyToClipboard" /> resolves with the copied text – tab-separated, one line per row. Pasted into
    Excel, Numbers or Google Sheets it lands in cells.
  </p>
  <LiveDemo name="selection-and-copy" title="Selection types" height={400}
            caption="Switch the type with the buttons. In “range” drag across cells, then press ⌘/Ctrl+C or “copy”." />

  <Callout type="version">
    <p>Since 1.1.88 hidden columns (here “Category”) are not copied and copying with nothing selected resolves instead of waiting
      forever. Since 1.1.90 every table gets its own selection model – before, tables without <code>getSelectionModel</code> shared one.</p>
  </Callout>

  <h2 id="paste">Cut and paste – with Excel</h2>
  <Callout type="version">
    <p>Cut and paste are new in 1.1.99.</p>
  </Callout>
  <p>
    With <ApiLink name="TableOptionsIf.clipboard" label="clipboard: true" /> the table answers the browser's own copy, cut
    and paste events: <kbd>Ctrl</kbd>/<kbd>⌘</kbd>+<kbd>C</kbd>, <kbd>X</kbd> and <kbd>V</kbd> – also from the browser menu.
    Excel and Google Sheets understand what it copies (text and an HTML table), and a block copied there lands in the
    table cell by cell: numbers become numbers, quotes and line breaks inside cells survive, a single value fills the whole
    selection. Only editable cells are written; text from outside runs through <code>editInputPipe</code>,
    <code>validate</code> always runs.
  </p>
  <Code lang="ts" code={`const selectionModel = new SelectionModel("range", "multi");
const tableOptions: TableOptionsIf = {
  ...new TableOptions(),
  getSelectionModel: () => selectionModel,
  editing: true,
  clipboard: { pasteAddsRows: true, createRow: () => ({ id: nextId(), quantity: 0 }) },
  undo: true                                  // a paste is one undo step
};
tableApi.pasteText("1\t2\n3\t4");             // the same from code`} />
  <p>
    Cut marks the cells with a dashed frame; they are cleared when you paste – one step, one undo. <ApiLink name="TableApi.cutSelection" />
    and <ApiLink name="TableApi.pasteText" /> do the same from your own buttons or menu.
  </p>

  <h2 id="next">Next</h2>
  <p>Clicks, double-clicks and a context menu of your own: <ChapterLink slug="events-and-context-menu" />.</p>
</TrainingLayout>
